# Who reviews changes to the paths that run, gate or steer the automation (#4915, step 2).
#
# This file only asks for the owner's review on a pull request that touches these paths. It does not block a merge:
# the ruleset does not require code-owner review, and the `owner-tap` label rule in scripts/merge_policy.py still
# decides what merges today. The last matching line wins, and every line names the same owner.
# scripts/tests/test_codeowners.py fails if a path the merge rules hold for the owner is left out.

# The pipeline: workflows, merge rules, trust rules and the runner and audit tooling.
/.github/                       @uncomposed
/scripts/lane_*.py              @uncomposed
/scripts/merge_policy.py        @uncomposed
/scripts/merge_queue_*.py       @uncomposed
/scripts/comment_trust.py       @uncomposed
/scripts/signoff_check.py       @uncomposed
/scripts/owner_tap_alert.py     @uncomposed
/ops/                           @uncomposed

# Text that agents read as instructions.
/AGENTS.md                      @uncomposed
/CLAUDE.md                      @uncomposed
/.claude/                       @uncomposed

# How the project takes contributions and security reports.
/CONTRIBUTING.md                @uncomposed
/SECURITY.md                    @uncomposed
